## HOW THE SOP WAS BORN — ORIGIN STORY

**Source file:** `V019 Claude Co Work Chat log.txt` (2,443 lines)
**First message:** Alan uploaded 16 documents + 8-step process for building a course framework.
**First checklist:** Message 3 — Alan explicitly requested: *"SOP means standard operating procedure + checklist / action list... listing everything i've prompted you with to do + your understanding of what needs to be done + how we do things and why"*

**The SOP v1 was born as a "grocery list"** with 6 sections:
- Section A: What the client instructed (18 items)
- Section B: Design decisions (10 items)
- Section C: What needs to be built (14 deliverables)
- Section D: How we build (12 process rules)
- Section E: Why we do it this way (10 principles)
- Section F: Client experience targets (10 targets)

**Evolution chain:**
v1 (6 sections, 18 A-items) → v2 (+Sections 0, G, H, I, 27 A-items) → v3.0 (+Section J: 86-item prompt audit, D18) → v3.1 (+POVP/D19, D20, Section L, status labels) → v3.2 (+PFV/D21, Section M) → v3.3 (+D22, error log Section N, build position) → v3.4 (+quick reference card, 6 tiers in G) → v3.5 (+D23, classroom map DFY/unlock/density markers) → v3.6 (+RC markers, WHY reconnection) → v3.7 (+D24, C1 sync, SOP confirmed ready) → v3.8 (+B12-B16, A53-A60, Doc #20 Clint Response, Blitz/Prime Protocol, 119 prompt items) → v3.9 (+D25-D28, sub-caches, Section O) → v3.9.1 (+D29, D30) → v3.9.2 (+D31, D32, backup system) → v3.9.3 (D27 refined: conservative thresholds + per-step inline + auto-continue)

